     "titulo": "The golden rule: V2",
     "texto": [
      "In an **affirmative main clause**, the conjugated verb usually takes second position. If another part of the sentence comes first, the subject goes after the verb:\n\n- **Jeg** bor her. → Her **bor jeg**.\n- **Det** regnede i går. → I går **regnede det**.\n\nUnlike English, where the subject usually comes first, this rule describes the position of the verb in a main clause; subordinate clauses have a different order."
